  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher expected policy rates increase the anticipated cost of capital for multi‑year infrastructure buildouts, disadvantaging smaller competitors and driving firms to centralize investment in large, well‑capitalized providers.</data>
