  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in market-implied volatility raises war‑risk and freight insurance premia and prompts shipowners and charterers to reroute, delay or idle voyages through high-risk stretches, directly increasing the rate of commercial shipping disruptions in the Gulf and nearby corridors.</data>
